course: dictionary
lesson: 1006
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word bolt is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
explain: «Leave a bike out in the rain all winter and its chain and bolts turn orange-brown and flaky.» Here the bolts are metal pins that hold parts together, like the nuts and bolts on a bike. Ask yourself: could a flash of lightning fit here? No, so this is a different meaning.
explain: «Thunder rumbles because sound from different parts of the long lightning bolt reaches you at different times.» Here a bolt is a flash of lightning. Try the swap: a flash of lightning makes sense in this sentence, so you have found the meaning.
explain: «When one horse in a field suddenly bolts, the whole herd thunders after it without stopping to ask why.» To bolt means to run away suddenly, like a frightened animal. The word suddenly is a clue, and so is the fear.
fact: A bolt can be a metal bar that slides across to lock a door or window.
fact: A bolt can also be a thick metal pin with a screw thread that goes with a nut to hold things together.
fact: «A bolt of lightning» is a flash of lightning in the sky.
fact: «Bolt» can also mean to run away suddenly, or to eat very fast: «Don't bolt your food or you might choke.»
fact: «Sits bolt upright» means sits very straight, suddenly, and «a bolt from the blue» means a total surprise.
exercise: «Leave a bike out in the rain all winter and its chain and bolts turn orange-brown and flaky.» What are the bolts on the bike? | Ways of running away quickly | Flashes of lightning in the sky | *Metal pins that hold parts together | Bars that slide across to lock a door
exercise: «Thunder rumbles because sound from different parts of the long lightning bolt reaches you at different times.» What is a bolt in this sentence? | To eat very fast | To run away like a frightened horse | *A flash of lightning | A metal bar on a door
exercise: «When one horse in a field suddenly bolts, the whole herd thunders after it.» What does bolts mean here? | *Runs away suddenly | Shines brightly in the dark | Locks itself in a stable | Eats its food very fast
test: «Don't bolt your food or you might choke.» What does bolt mean in this sentence? | To lock with a bolt | A flash of lightning | To run away like a frightened horse | *To eat very fast
test: Someone who sits bolt upright sits very straight, suddenly. What does bolt upright mean? | Lying down flat in bed | Slowly and sleepily | Upside down on the floor | *Very straight, suddenly
exam: «Please bolt the door before you go to bed.» What does bolt mean in this sentence? | To eat very fast | To run away suddenly like a horse | A flash of lightning in the sky | *To lock with a bolt
